   "text": "Fig. 8.1 shows an ammeter connected to a coil wound on a thin plastic cylinder. A small\ntrolley is placed on a curved track which passes through the cylinder.\nA\ntrolley\ncylinder\ntrack\nThe trolley is released from the position shown in Fig. 8.1. It travels through the coil from right\nto left. The trolley travels back from left to right. It has a lower maximum speed when it travels\nfrom left to right.\nThe plastic cylinder does not affect any magnetic field. A magnet is fixed to the trolley.",
